  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Set at the Nouveau Port in Cavalaire, La Suite serves world cuisine with Italian influences, in an air-conditioned setting extended by a large terrace with harbour views.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>⚠️ Only the PagesJaunes/Mappy directory says "pets accepted"; the Cavalaire-sur-Mer tourist office (2025-2026 brochure, which lists La Suite among its bars and restaurants) and the restaurant publish no rule on dogs (not to be confused with "Le Bateau Ivre", another restaurant at the Nouveau Port that officially confirms it accepts pets). Better to call before going with your dog than to rely on unverified information. Budget around €21-30 for the meal. The air-conditioned dining room is a real plus on hot days, and the available wifi lets you extend your stay if needed.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: dog access here rests on a directory only — call before you come, or try Le Bateau Ivre instead, a little further along the same harbour, which officially confirms it accepts pets.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cavalaire harbour and its promenade are right nearby, perfect for a digestive walk with your dog before or after the meal.</p>
